WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:02.940
The seas of space belong to everyone.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.820
Since ancient times, the sea has turned boys into men.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.360
In the same way, it now trains young women.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.240
With their sudden introduction to the business of piracy,

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:20.040
the girls have been tossed into stormy seas, becoming sailors.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.920
There's also the word "relaxation,"
which means the same thing as "rest."

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.740
Gruier, being a pirate was fun, wasn't it?

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.860
I reminded Marika to call us again

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.530
should another chance for us to do it arise.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:26.540
Gruier, you're such good friends with her.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.750
Yes.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.830
Things are never boring when she's around.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:36.800
You go to the same school, and you're in the same club, but you're still a princess and a pirate.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.890
I don't think it's good to get too close.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:46.720
Is it a problem too large for even
the Serenity royal family to handle?

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.810
A-Anyway, I only want...

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:57.780
Thinking back, it probably wasn't a coincidence that Sir Gonzaemon gave me that ID ring for the Bentenmaru.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.320
What do you mean?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:05.580
We were bonded by fate, destined to meet one another in this vast universe.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.330
Bonded, huh?

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.880
Marika, eat your food.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.050
I'd rather sleep than eat.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.300
Like how you feel the day after an exam?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.180
Yeah, that's it.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.050
I don't feel like doing anything.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.640
Just relaxing...

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:31.310
So, now that she's on land,
the space pirate is sunbathing?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.810
Yup.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.190
You'll dry right out.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.070
That's fine.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.370
Once you get used to it, this place ain't so bad.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.410
Yeah.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.830
This military hospital isn't as bad as I expected.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.420
The food's bad though.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.880
Well, we got paid just to sleep.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.790
It's all good.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.490
It worries me that the captain hasn't done anything since then.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.590
It's fine.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.640
She's relaxing too.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.140
Rest is important, once in a while.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.390
I hope she doesn't relax too much.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.610
Now, let's get to the relay station!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.820
Right!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.110
We don't have many more shuttle
tickets for the yacht club this year.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.620
I'm not sure why they look like this, but whatever.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.200
Let's get up there and do it!

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.120
Right!

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.880
Get to it, ladies!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.640
Right!

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.520
The practice cruise, the piracy...

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.030
How many times have we been
to the relay station this year?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.990
We've been here so often it's like we're sailors!

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.870
No! We are sailors!

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.040
This ship is really well-maintained given its age.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.960
It's still in working order.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.380
We should thank all our seniors.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.000
I'll do my best to clean it up.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.250
Out of the way!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.840
Wait!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.340
Lock Released.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.220
Dinghies!

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.980
I didn't know we had a dinghy.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.350
Of course we do. We're the yacht club.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.190
I've never seen one before.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.150
I don't think I have either.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:47.240
They're a little old, but they're nice ships.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.280
President, can I take them out?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.620
Out to do what?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.120
I want to pilot them.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.960
Sure, I guess.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.580
We'll put them in the shuttle later.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.130
Great!

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.630
I'll clean you all up, okay?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.130
Where to start?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:09.340
Thirty minutes left! Let's finish up right!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.140
Yeah!

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.520
So, it went by fast, but the first day is over!

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.940
Good work, everyone!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.770
So tired...

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:25.400
President, I'm gonna stay at the station to clean the Bentenmaru a little.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.240
Okay.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.240
Wait... Sure you wanna do it alone?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.030
Want help?

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.620
Thanks, Gruier.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.240
I'll ask you when I collapse.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.040
I'll be waiting for you to collapse sooner.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:43.790
Once I get a little further along, you can all help.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.300
I've come all the way up into space,

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.560
so I need to get some work done.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.060
This is control.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.310
Hakuoh Academy Transport,

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.190
we show no flight plan for you.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.810
What is your bearing?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.820
This is the pirate ship Bentenmaru's captain, Kato Marika.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.200
I'm heading to the Bentenmaru.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.070
Sending flight plan now.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.780
We've received it.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.990
Roger.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.760
By the way, Captain...

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.580
I saw the news.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.080
Thanks.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.590
I'm concerned about Misa and the crew not saying anything though...

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.060
Someone's visiting the Bentenmaru.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.690
A thief?

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.070
The captain.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.570
She just can't stay put, can she?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.360
Is she sending the ship out again?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.120
She's alone, so probably not.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.740
Let's see what she does.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.080
I win. Four concealed triplets.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.760
Until it's a bit cleaner,

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.850
I don't really think I could ask the
yacht club or the crew for help.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.350
I have to keep the Bentenmaru's image in mind.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.030
Ugh.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.290
Is this some junk the yacht club brought aboard,

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.290
or stuff belonging to the crew?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.290
I can't even tell anymore.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.630
Ah, I know.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.340
That's a great idea.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.260
Gravity System Active

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:04.230
Behold the power of zero-g!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.230
Crap!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:09.860
Moving garbage,
gravity off!
Collecting garbage,
gravity on!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.860
There's an order to it!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.070
Jeez...

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.610
I should have asked Lilly, Ursula, and them to help.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.870
They made the biggest mess.

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:36.340
I'll call it Operation Dust G!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.550
Oh no!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.770
Gotta get back!

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.150
The last shuttle to Sea of the Morningstar...

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.190
Wait!

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.150
will be departing shortly.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.650
Wait! Wait!

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:56.650
Anyone who has not yet completed their boarding papers, please hurry.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.860
Uh-oh...

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.410
I forgot to lock the entrance.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.370
Oh well.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.830
I set the master lock on the system.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.420
Tomorrow...

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.640
Hey, master...

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.800
See ya tomorrow.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.640
It's tomorrow!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.360
Time for day two of cleaning!

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:58.920
Marika, a female double for a bullet terminal please.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:00.930
Marika, a female double?

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.680
Sorry, I was spacing out.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.190
Ow...

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.560
Are you all right?

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.150
You don't seem quite yourself.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.780
Do you have a fever?

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.490
Maybe I'm coming down with that cat-monkey cold...

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.240
You're just worn out.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.740
So much <i>has</i> happened.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:24.490
Yeah...

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.500
Cleaning sure is hard.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.040
The engine room safety relay?

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:52.770
Yeah.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:55.650
It looks old.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.150
We don't have a spare?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.240
I guess this was the last one.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.530
I see.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.280
Fine.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.280
Want to try repairing it with junk from the club room?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:06.780
Sure.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.870
Okay, back to work on the Bentenmaru.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.800
I'll finish this today!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.950
I don't know if this is junk or someone's stuff.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.250
I'll have them sort it.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.580
I'm done.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:53.460
Okay.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.710
All right!

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.960
I'll move the containers to the yacht club warehouse!

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:09.470
<i>We're white cranes. The white...</i>

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.270
Misa, what is it at this hour?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.850
You're being discharged?

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.520
Yup, that's right.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.440
It was sudden, so everyone's rushing.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.190
When?

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.150
When do you leave?

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:22.990
Tomorrow!

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:24.950
Should I prepare a homecoming party?

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.320
Nah.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.870
After school, just undo the master lock on the Bentenmaru.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:30.490
Okay,

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.290
will do.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.490
Goodnight.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:37.500
We will be arriving at New Okuhama Airport shortly.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.970
This is nice.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:48.340
It's especially good today.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.760
Is it?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:50.760
Yeah.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:55.890
Maybe it's time that you started making the pot-au-feu.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.560
You'll teach me?

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:05.490
If you're the Bentenmaru's captain, that means you've inherited the Kato family secrets.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.660
You should already be able to make it.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:20.000
I thought we could find the parts in the club room.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.880
What is all this stuff doing here, anyway?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.510
Oh well.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.300
Just leave it for now.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.220
I'll close it up.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.390
Okay.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.810
We have no choice.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.640
We'll have to ask the fabrication club to make us the parts.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.180
It'll cost a ton.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.440
Misa, have you reached the Bentenmaru?

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.650
I'll be there soon—

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.230
Not soon! Now!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.950
It's good to see you all.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:53.370
Captain!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.790
Welcome back, everyone.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:56.950
Greet later.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.500
Release the master lock.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:00.460
The lock?

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.710
Oh, right. The gravity's still off.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.710
Why?

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:08.470
The bridge controls are locked.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.180
We made it from the hatch to the bridge, but...

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.300
Unlock it now, please.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.640
We'll discuss you forgetting to lock the door afterwards.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:18.890
Jeez.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.190
Did you listen to me at all yesterday?

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.860
Sorry, sorry.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:24.570
Oh?

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.230
Huh? Huh...

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.070
Oh, yeah!

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.490
I put it in my club parka!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.070
Uh-oh...

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.370
For better or worse, I never took it out.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:42.080
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.210
Your ID ring is gone?!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.050
Ring... Ring, where are you?

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.130
We can't use the ship as it is.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.590
But...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.140
Where'd you drop it?

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.800
If I knew, I wouldn't be looking!

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:58.180
You should've just kept it on your finger.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.310
It's for a man, so it's too large.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:06.610
Then, to summarize, yesterday was the last time the captain used the master lock.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:10.860
She probably dropped it during her club duties.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.110
Remember what you were doing!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.240
I'm trying, but...

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.120
It's gotta be somewhere.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.500
What if I dropped it somewhere else?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.830
As long as you didn't drop it in space, it'll be fine.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:26.290
If we retrace your actions, we'll find it.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.740
Wh-What should I do?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.010
No...

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.510
I want to give it to you.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:34.970
Please accept it.

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:38.470
All right.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.640
Some thanks, huh?

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.270
You appear to be in some trouble.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.860
We'll help you.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.990
Bentenmaru, boot up!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.000
Master lock disabled.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:07.830
System operational.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.090
Radar sensor okay. Nothing unusual.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.090
Helm on-line.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.260
Primary and sub-engines stabilized.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.800
Comm systems...

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:16.800
All green.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:20.430
Weapon and control systems primed for combat.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.520
Now...

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.940
Time for some piracy!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.310
No, no, no!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:28.940
What are you all doing?

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:33.320
We heard you were in trouble, so we came.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:36.150
Heard I was in trouble?

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.320
Grunhilde,

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.310
where did you hear that?

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.910
The Silent Whisper, huh?

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:45.330
With keen ears like that, hearing would be a piece of cake.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.960
Cake!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.790
Marika, the captain's seat is yours.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:50.790
And this ring...

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.800
You dropped it on the Odette II.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:58.180
Thank you.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:01.510
I'm amazed you recognized it as the
Bentenmaru administrator's ID ring.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:05.310
The president helped me analyze it.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.980
Don't drop something that valuable.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.800
The Galactic Empire might have gotten involved.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.230
It's that bad?

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.740
I'm upset!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.030
That is the sign of our bond,
given to me by Sir Gonzaemon.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:20.990
Bond?

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.950
The bond between you, me, and Sir Gonzaemon.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.960
And you, Hilde... All four of us.

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.090
Yeah.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.750
That's right.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.920
Thanks so much,

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.210
you guys.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.930
Yep.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.440
Not bad, yacht club.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.230
They had a good advisor.

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:54.780
She joined while you were gone.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.190
There it is, my doll!

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.700
Is that a special rare?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.450
San-Daime, do you collect them too?

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.950
Wanna trade?

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.370
Seriously?

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.870
You there... Get to work.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:11.000
You're the one who made a mess of everything.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:13.170
No whining!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.840
Or I'll lower the weight limit for personal effects.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.220
No! No!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.760
Stupid captain!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.890
I'm not tuning alpha and beta for you anymore!

